@startuml class-diagram-modules
title UML Class / Component View - Backend functional modules and the models they use
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members
left to right direction

legend top left
  Companion to class-diagram.puml. The backend is plain CommonJS modules, not classes;
  <<module>> boxes show real require() dependencies only. Model boxes are the
  Mongoose models from class-diagram.puml (attributes omitted here).
endlegend

class User <<Mongoose model>>
class Job <<Mongoose model>>
class Application <<Mongoose model>>

  class authController <<module>>
  class applicantController <<module>>
  class companyController <<module>>
  class adminController <<module>>
  class jobController <<module>>
  class authMiddleware <<module>> {
    +authMiddleware(req, res, next)
  }
  class roleMiddleware <<module>> {
    +roleMiddleware(...roles)
  }
  class helpers <<module>> {
    +generateOTP() : String
    +generateAccessToken(payload) : String
    +isValidEmail(email) : Boolean
    +isStrongPassword(pw) : Boolean
    +makeSlug(...parts) : String
    +makeInitials(name) : String
    +toList(value, sep) : String[]
    +formatJob(job) : Object
    +statusLabel(status) : String
    +daysLeft(deadline) : Number
  }
  class mailService <<module>> {
    +sendMail({email, subject, otp}) : Promise
  }
  class uploadToCloudinary <<module>> {
    +uploadToCloudinary(file, folder) : Promise
    +deleteFromCloudinary(publicId, type) : Promise
  }

authController ..> User
authController ..> helpers
authController ..> mailService
authController ..> uploadToCloudinary
applicantController ..> Job
applicantController ..> Application
applicantController ..> uploadToCloudinary
companyController ..> Job
companyController ..> Application
companyController ..> helpers
companyController ..> uploadToCloudinary
adminController ..> User
adminController ..> Job
adminController ..> Application
adminController ..> uploadToCloudinary
adminController ..> helpers
jobController ..> Job
jobController ..> User
jobController ..> helpers
authMiddleware ..> User
note right of authMiddleware : verifies the accessToken cookie with jsonwebtoken (JWT_SEC)\nand loads User; does not use helpers
@enduml
